course: dictionary
lesson: 2079
title: Constrictors: animals that squeeze
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A constrictor is a snake that hunts by wrapping its body around its prey and squeezing. Boas and pythons are famous constrictors. «They have no venom; they hunt by grabbing prey and wrapping it in their coils, which is why they are called constrictors.» The name tells you what they do: they constrict, which means they squeeze tighter and tighter.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «Constrictors coil around prey and tighten each time it breathes out.» Coil and tighten are the clues. A constrictor squeezes harder when its prey breathes out, so the animal cannot get a full breath. Always check your meaning by putting it back in the sentence: a constrictor is a snake that squeezes its prey, and that still makes sense.
explain: The word can mean more than one thing. In a body lesson, a constrictor is a muscle that tightens or narrows a part of the body, such as the throat. Anything that squeezes or narrows something can also be called a constrictor. When a word has more than one meaning, read the sentence around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: A constrictor is a snake that kills its prey by wrapping its body around it and squeezing.
fact: Boa constrictors and pythons are both constrictors.
fact: Constrictors have no venom. They hunt by squeezing, not by biting with poison.
fact: «Pythons and boas are constrictors that squeeze prey so its blood stops flowing.»
fact: The reticulated python is over 6 metres long, and it is the longest snake.
exercise: «Pythons and boas are constrictors that squeeze prey so its blood stops flowing.» What is a constrictor? | A bird that sings at dawn | *A snake that kills by wrapping its body around prey and squeezing | A tool for cutting wire | A fish with a sharp tail
exercise: «They have no venom; they hunt by grabbing prey and wrapping it in their coils.» Which word tells you that an animal injects poison? | coils | *venom | prey | grabbing
exercise: In «Constrictors coil around prey and tighten each time it breathes out», find and copy one word that means the animal being hunted. | breathes | coil | *prey | tighten
test: In a body lesson, what does a constrictor muscle do? | *Tightens or narrows a part of the body, such as the throat | Pushes air out of the lungs | Makes you laugh | Carries food to the stomach
test: «The boa constrictor wrapped itself around the branch and squeezed.» Why is it called a constrictor? | Because it lives in water | Because it has a sharp tail | *Because it squeezes its prey | Because it sings loudly
exam: «Constrictors have no venom», the sentence tells you. What does a constrictor use to kill its prey instead of poison? | *Squeezing and wrapping its coils around the prey | Its teeth only | Loud noises | A sharp tail
